---
description: What must never reach a tracked file, a commit or a pull request
alwaysApply: true
---

This repository is public. The working session that produces the work is not, and the
boundary is one way. Tracked files, commit messages, pull requests, issues and code comments
state technical requirements, in the product's own words, and nothing else.

Reference material shared during development is for reading, not for keeping. Take the
requirement out of it, state the requirement in the product's own words, and let the
reference go.

The full rule, and everything else that governs work here, is in `AGENTS.md`. Read it, and
read `AGENTS.local.md` if it exists (it is private and untracked). `python3
Scripts/disclosure_audit.py` enforces the rule and runs in `make verify`, in the pre-push and
commit-msg hooks, and on every pull request.
